<title>JAPAN: U.S. says no progress in port dispute with Japan.</title>
<headline>U.S. says no progress in port dispute with Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States has yet to see any progress in its dispute with Japan over Japanese port practices, a U.S. embassy official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In November, the U.S. Federal Maritime Commission (FMC) announced plans to impose sanctions on three Japanese shipping firms. The announcement was followed by a sixty day comment period which ended on January 20.</p>
<p>The official said the FMC was still considering those comments, although a decision was expected &quot;very soon&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;If there were real signs of progress that would be the most effective way of persuading the FMC not to go ahead but right now we don't see those signs,&quot; said the official.</p>
</text>
